### Redirection
0 - stdin
1 - stdout
2 - stderr

18. data 1>file_name.txt - this overwrite the file of data command in file_name.txt if exist if not exist create one
19. data 1>>file_name.txt - this doesn't overwrite but append the output to file.
20. data 1>>output_name.txt 2>>error_name.txt  - append output respectively output in output_name.txt and error in error_name.txt
21. ls error_name.txt error.txt >> newfile.txt 2>&1 - this give both error and output message at the same life newfile.txt. 

### Piping
Piping helps to specify what to do with the command.

22. cat file.txt | grep a - this will open the file.txt and just display the lines which have a (grep help to grab the specific value)
23. ls -a | tee redirect.txt - first display the value and the redirect the value to the file.
24. cat file.txt|more - help to view the content of file but only one direct down words.
25. cat file.txt|less - help to view the content of file updown all direction.


26. head file.txt - give first 10 lines of the file.
27. tail file.txt - give last 10 lines of the file.
28. tail -f file.txt - give the lastest modified lines of the file.


### File management
29. cp file1.txt file2.txt - copy the content of file1 to file2
30. mv /a/file.txt /b - this moves file.txt from /a ditectory to /b and delete it from /a but not permanently still files are found in harddrive
31. mv file1.txt file2.txt - this change the name of the file
32. shred -u file.txt - delete the file permanently.
33. mkdir /text - make a directory.
34. rmdir /text - remove and empty directory.
35. rm -i - remove directory and files within directory with prompts
36. rm -rf - remove without prompt
